Z||000000||stimpy||01-19-2001||10:34 PM||||Saw your comment in neverfinished's thread about using WebTV<BR>Phil, you can use WebTV to post pics on the forum. You just can't use the PIP to hold your images. Don't fear, just store your images on Photopoint, and store your Photopoint album in Favorites. When you have a thread you want to post on, go to favorites, find your image (click til you get the black background) then hit your "go to" key. Arrow down to "show current and click. It will show the location of the pic you are looking at. Hit "cmd"A to highlight the address, then hit "cmd"C to copy. You'll hear a click. Then hit "Recent" to go back to your thread and use the <BR>"[ img ][ /img ]" tags(without extra spaces in the brackets) on either side of your cursor, then hit "cmd"V to paste the location of your image between the tags. Voila, your image is posted.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||10
Z||000001||Philphine||01-19-2001||11:06 PM||||ok.. i read it 5 or 6 times and i still don't understand. i'm kinda dence. how do i get the pictures on photopoint? do i need another computer to get them on? maybe if i can get that far i can work at it from there. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||AL||01-20-2001||04:47 AM||||if you have a camcorder tape your ca on a tape,then connect it to your web tv and when you send the email to photopoint push picture,then add it to you email and send it to photopoint,then get i photopoint find the pic you want and push info on the key board ,then push cmd and a at the same time,  and then push cmd and c at the same time and you have cut the listing. now go to the forum and push cmd and c again,you will see the info pasted and then just add [img] before the http and [/img] at the end and then hit sig boxs and presto you have a pic on the forum<B>al</B>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/AL_sig.gif">  <BR>86gt fastback ported and polished heads,k&n air filter holley side scoop,deck lid scoop.<BR>84 indy fiero<P>------------------<BR> <p>[This message has been edited by AL (edited 01-20-2001).]||||reg||1
